==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA| [bɪ'spiːk]}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|bespeaks|bespeaking|'''[[bespoke]]''' or '''[[bespake]]''' (archaic)|'''[[bespoken]]''' or '''[[bespoke]]''' (archaic)}}

# To [[order]] or [[reserve]] [[in advance]].

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A request for a specific performance, by a patron.

===Quotations===
* '''1839''', Charles Dickens, ''[[w:Nicholas Nickleby|Nicholas Nickleby]]''
*: "By the bye, I've been thinking of bringing out that piece of yours on her '''bespeak''' night."
*: "When?", asked Nicholas.
*: "The night of her '''bespeak'''. Her benefit night. When her friends and patrons '''bespeak''' the play."
*: "Oh! I understand", replied Nicholas.

